         libxinerama1,
         libxkbcommon0,
         libxrandr2,
         libxrender1
Recommends: libpulse0,
            libdecor-0-0,
            libdbus-1-3,
            libfontconfig1,
            libvulkan1
Suggests: libspeechd2
Conflicts: omadungeon
Replaces: omadungeon
Provides: omadungeon (= ${binary:Version})
Description: rogue-like dungeon crawler skinned by your Omarchy theme (no music)
 Omadungeon is a fast, room-based rogue-like whose palette, lighting and level
 generation are derived from the Omarchy theme and wallpaper you are currently
 running. Switch theme and the dungeon retints in front of you, and the next
 floor generates differently. The enemies are the people who dislike your
 setup: clowns, greybeards and tinkerers.
 .
 Runs are short and build-driven. Rooms lock until they are cleared, a chest
 appears after every fight, and a character comes together from stats,
 procedural loot and two active plus two passive ability slots. Four classes -
 Fighter, Ranger, Wizard and Oligarch - each bring a starting weapon, an innate
 passive, a unique dodge and a class ability. Nine floors span three biomes
 with a boss every third floor, and quitting is safe: a run resumes where you
 left the room. Keyboard and mouse and controller input are both first class.
 .
 This is the lite build: it is the same game as the omadungeon package with the
 bundled Omarchy Radio soundtrack left out, which takes it from roughly 230 MB
 installed to roughly 70 MB. Sound effects and the generated score are still
 present, as is the built-in fallback score; only the Omarchy Radio playlist
 is absent, so the credits screen lists no tracks and the music-derived
 generation and lighting lever falls back to its neutral default. Install
 omadungeon instead if you want the soundtrack.
